<title>USA: Alabama National BanCorp Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Alabama National BanCorp Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			     Three Months Ended   Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				 September 30,	  September 30,</p>
<p>				1996	   1995     1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net interest income$   8,796   $   4,754 $ 25,789   $ 13,726</p>
<p>Provision for loan</p>
<p>  losses			  -	   202	209	  210</p>
<p> Net income		 2,585	 1,019    6,942	3,704</p>
<p>Net income per common</p>
<p>   share(1)		  0.39	  0.15     1.04	 1.05</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>and common equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding    6,679	 2,874    6,675	2,874</p>
<p>					    September 30, September 30,</p>
<p>							 1996	    1995</p>
<p> Total assets				   $841,191     $515,522</p>
<p> Deposits					  668,225	413,339</p>
<p>NOTE - Per common share data is calculated based upon net income as adjusted for cash dividends paid on preferred stock of $4,000 and $600,000 for the three months ended September 30, 1996 and 1995, and $4,000 and $679,000 for the nine months ended September 30, 1996 and 1995.  </p>
<p>1996 Q3 results include a one-time, pre-tax charge of $667,000 related to the special assessment by the Savings Association Insurance Fund. The charge was offset by non-operating income in the quarter from the resolution of a previous credit problem and existing other reserves.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
